            "instrument": "python_module",
            "label": "compiled dynamics and pulse-braking probe",
            "module": "robot_learning.lab.dynamics_probe"
          }
        ],
        "rationale": "The initial model makes dynamic authority versus stabilization the first decision-relevant distinction, but compiled inertias and effective motor authority are unresolved. This measurement separates a low-authority or poorly conditioned reach mechanism from a high-velocity overshoot and braking mechanism before spending the startup allocation on a confounded learned policy. Joint-limit margins and Jacobian singular values also test whether branch and radial geometry must condition the next intervention."
      },
